<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1980</h1><p class="ref-lede">1980 in world history: 12 events, 3 births, 20 deaths and 2 states that came to an end. 199 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1976">1976</a><a href="/years/1977">1977</a><a href="/years/1978">1978</a><a href="/years/1979">1979</a><a href="/years/1980" aria-current="page">1980</a><a href="/years/1981">1981</a><a href="/years/1982">1982</a><a href="/years/1983">1983</a><a href="/years/1984">1984</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-22">22 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US amateurs beat the Soviet Union in the 'Miracle on Ice'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A team of American college players defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, four-time Olympic champions, 4-3 at the Lake Placid Winter Olympics. The US went on to win the gold medal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-27">27 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts for the first time in 123 years</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A steam explosion blasted a crater in the summit of the Washington volcano after a week of earthquakes. On 18 May a massive eruption tore away its north face and killed 57 people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-18">18 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts in Washington State</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake triggered a vast landslide and lateral blast that tore away the mountain's north face. Fifty-seven people died in the deadliest eruption in US history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-1">1 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">CNN launches as the first 24-hour news channel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ted Turner's Cable News Network began broadcasting from Atlanta. Its round-the-clock coverage created the modern continuous news cycle.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-22">22 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Iran</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>'s forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, starting an eight-year war of trenches, missile attacks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poison-gas">poison gas</a>. Hundreds of thousands died before a ceasefire in 1988 left borders unchanged.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-8">8 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon is shot dead in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Mark <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Chapman shot John Lennon outside the Dakota building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>. The killing of the former Beatle prompted vigils around the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift">Mariel boatlift</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mariel boatlift was the mass emigration of about 125,000 Cubans from the port of Mariel to Florida between April and October 1980.</p></div></li></ol></section>
